advertised metadata (the builtin table row)
-------------------------------------------

name          repl_timeout
description   "Set the per-step timeout in seconds for one REPL
              (0 = unlimited; default 10s). Applies to repl_step,
              repl_edit, repl_replay and repl_merge re-execution.
              DO NOT raise it above 10s without a specific reason:
              calls like metis, auto, blast, force should finish in
              5s, and a step that needs longer usually points at a
              proof that ought to be broken down. Forked REPLs
              inherit the parent's timeout at fork time."
              (source: mcp_server.py timeout :388 verbatim, plus the
              fork-inheritance fact from ir.ML:456.)
inputSchema   {"type": "object",
               "properties": {
                 "repl": {"type": "string"},
                 "secs": {"type": "integer"}},
               "required": ["repl", "secs"]}
annotations   {"readOnlyHint": false, "idempotentHint": true,
               "openWorldHint": false}
              (setting the same value twice is a no-op — honest
              idempotency, like repl_replay.)
outputSchema  none.

