assumptions and how to test them
--------------------------------

T1  the set value actually bounds steps: secs=1 makes a sleeping
    step fail, 0 makes it run to completion.
    test [ml unit]: timeout 1 + slow step -> timeout error;
    timeout 0 + the same step -> ok. (keep the sleep short — this is
    the same fixture as plans/repl_step T3.)
T2  negative secs: pin the engine behavior while implementing —
    likely accepted and nonsensical; if so, reject scala-side
    (schema minimum: 0 is advisory only) or engine-side, and test
    the chosen gate.
    test [ml unit]: timeout -1 -> the pinned behavior.
T3  show reflects it ("timeout=5s" / "unlimited").
    test [ml unit]: set, show -> string present.
T4  full chain.
    test [bridge]: session.ir("timeout", ...) -> ok reply.

