landed: done (2026-07-09). T1..T4 green at all layers. T1 confirmed the
set value bounds steps: secs=1 makes a 2s sleeping step time out
("timed out"), secs=0 lets the same step run to completion. T2's engine
behavior is now pinned, with a genuine surprise on the RENDERING side:
exec_text only bounds execution when timeout_secs > 0 (ir.ML:342), so a
negative value behaves exactly like 0/unlimited for step execution --
a slow step under timeout -1 still succeeds. But show's string only
special-cases exactly 0 as "unlimited" (ir.ML:537); any other value,
negative included, goes through SML's plain \<^ML>\<open>string_of_int\<close>,
which spells negative numbers with a tilde, not a minus sign -- so
repl_show reports "timeout=~1s" for a REPL set to -1, not "timeout=-1s"
as a JSON-facing caller might expect. Both halves (execution treats
negative as unlimited; display does not) are pinned in the test. T3
confirmed show's normal rendering: "timeout=Ns" for a positive value,
"timeout=unlimited" for 0. T4 (bridge + e2e) confirmed the full chain
against both a headless PIDE session and a live server: repl_timeout's
reply names the new value, and repl_show immediately reflects it. ml
